\ MM-14 1.x spellings keep working: upper-case control words and control
\ flow outside definitions. The whole rest of the line runs as one unit.
: count10 10 0 DO I . LOOP ;
count10
3 0 DO I LOOP .s clst
0 IF 5 THEN depth .
1 IF 7 THEN .
0 IF 1 ELSE 2 THEN .
: nest 1 IF 0 IF 11 ELSE 22 THEN 33 ELSE 44 THEN ;
nest .s clst
: ml DO I sin . LOOP ;
3 0 ml
\ an error inside top-level control flow rolls the whole line back
1 2 3 0 do i 0 / loop
.s clst
\ unterminated control at top level is a compile error, nothing runs
5 if 1 2 3
.s
\ mixed case works too
2 0 Do I Loop .s clst
\ control words cannot be redefined under either spelling
: DO 1 ;
: Loop 1 ;
